 "no_published_reason": null,
 "differences": [
  "For two participants (S42 and S47 in the deposit) the deposit's two spreadsheets disagree on the paretic and dominant side; the 'Further Data' sheet (the one that also holds time since stroke) was used.",
  "The paper reports a mean time since stroke of 39 months for the mild group; the deposit gives 41.9 (the paper's Table 1 lists 8 months for the participant whom the deposit lists at 51). The paper reports 7 right and 8 left paretic arms in the mild group; the deposit's 'Further Data' sheet gives 8 right. The severe-group values and all other group numbers reproduce.",
  "The Zenodo record 7587404 is titled 'Informing upper extremity rehabilitation through endpoint kinematics of the functional reaching movement after stroke' (Jan 2023, CC BY 4.0, with the same participants); the PeerJ paper's own data statement points to a later record, 10.5281/zenodo.7968664 (May 2023, 'Upper extremity kinematics: Development of a quantitative measure of impairment severity and dissimilarity after stroke', CC BY 4.0). The PeerJ paper is cited here because the groups, ages and reach capacities match it.",
  "One file header in S53 states 166895 frames but the sheet holds 45158 rows; the rows present are converted."
 ],
